# ASP Bot — Setup Reference

## Repo settings
- Repo must be **Public** (unlimited Actions minutes on free plan)
- Actions must be enabled: Settings → Actions → General → Allow all

## Required Global Secrets
| Name | Description |
|------|-------------|
| GH_PAT | GitHub Personal Access Token (repo scope) |
| GMAIL_EMAIL | Your Gmail address |
| GMAIL_APP_PW | Gmail App Password (16 chars, no spaces) |
| FB_ACCOUNTS | Facebook accounts (one `email:password` per line) |
| CONTENT | Default posts (one per line) — used if CONTENT_N not set |
| IMAGES | Default image URLs (one per line) |
| COMMENTS | Comments to leave in groups (one per line) |

## Optional Per-Account Secrets
- `CONTENT_1` .. `CONTENT_10` — niche-specific posts
- `IMAGES_1` .. `IMAGES_10` — niche-specific images

## Auto-Managed Secrets (do not edit manually)
- `FB_COOKIES_1` .. `FB_COOKIES_N` — created by "Add Account (Auto)"

## Setup Order
1. Paste all 10 files into repo
2. Make repo Public
3. Add global secrets (7 above)
4. Add FB_ACCOUNTS with your first accounts
5. Actions → "Add Account (Auto)" → Run workflow (leave inputs empty)
6. Actions → "Group Discovery" → Run workflow (populates groups.txt)
7. Wait — Auto Poster runs on cron 15x/day

## Adding More Accounts
1. Update FB_ACCOUNTS secret (append new `email:password` lines)
2. Actions → "Add Account (Auto)" → Run workflow (leave inputs empty)
3. Only new accounts get processed

## Updating Content
- Just update `CONTENT` or `CONTENT_N` secret
- Changes apply on next cron run (no re-deploy needed)

## Monitoring
- Actions tab shows all runs
- `state/acc{N}.json` shows per-account progress
- `groups.txt` shows discovered groups
